<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - FRAME YR SHR SLIPS, DIV CUT.</title>
<headline>TABLE - FRAME YR SHR SLIPS, DIV CUT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)	 </p>
<p>    - headline		 110.0     vs    125.0</p>
<p>    - attrib		   152.0     vs    176.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   21.0     vs    24.0  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	    32.12     vs    37.67</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    71.35     vs    82.75</p>
<p>    Tax			  23.34     vs    26.48</p>
<p>Div and </p>
<p>    interest income	  14.46     vs    8.95</p>
<p>    Turnover		  730.89     vs    807.90</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 7.21     vs    14.29</p>
<p>Full name: Frame group Holdings Ltd (clothing, footwear and</p>
<p>textiles)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said market conditions were mixed and</p>
<p>volatile in the retail sector but it had seen strong demand for</p>
<p>several of its products in the fourth quarter and on balance</p>
<p>order books continued to look relatively healthy. </p>
<p>It said the property division made a meaningful contribution</p>
<p>to group income and was expected to grow substantially during</p>
<p>the coming year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
